vitrine.options.view_distance.tooltip=The render distance controls how far away terrain will be rendered. Shorter distances mean that less terrain will be rendered, improving frame rates.
vitrine.options.brightness.tooltip=Controls the brightness (gamma) of the game.
vitrine.options.clouds.name=Clouds
vitrine.options.clouds.tooltip=Controls whether or not clouds will be visible.
vitrine.options.gui_scale.tooltip=Sets the maximum scale factor to be used for the user interface. If 'auto' is used, then the largest scale factor will always be used.
vitrine.options.fullscreen.tooltip=If enabled, the game will display in full-screen (if supported).
vitrine.options.v_sync.tooltip=If enabled, the game's frame rate will be synchronized to the monitor's refresh rate, making for a generally smoother experience at the expense of overall input latency. This setting might reduce performance if your system is too slow.
vitrine.options.fps_limit.tooltip=Limits the maximum number of frames per second. This can help reduce battery usage and general system load when multi-tasking. If V-Sync is enabled, this option will be ignored unless it is lower than your display's refresh rate.
vitrine.options.view_bobbing.tooltip=If enabled, the player's view will sway and bob when moving around. Players who experience motion sickness while playing can benefit from disabling this.
vitrine.options.attack_indicator.tooltip=Controls where the Attack Indicator is displayed on screen.
vitrine.options.graphics_quality.tooltip=The default graphics quality controls some legacy options and is necessary for mod compatibility. If the options below are left to "Default", they will use this setting.
vitrine.options.clouds_quality.tooltip=Controls the quality of rendered clouds in the sky.
vitrine.options.weather_quality.tooltip=Controls the quality of rain and snow effects.
vitrine.options.leaves_quality.name=Leaves Quality
vitrine.options.leaves_quality.tooltip=Controls the quality of leaves.
vitrine.options.particle_quality.tooltip=Controls the maximum number of particles which can be present on screen at any one time.
vitrine.options.smooth_lighting.tooltip=Controls whether blocks will be smoothly lit and shaded. This slightly increases the amount of time needed to re-build a chunk, but doesn't affect frame rates.
vitrine.options.biome_blend.name=Biome Blend
vitrine.options.biome_blend.value=%s block(s)
vitrine.options.biome_blend.tooltip=Controls the range which biomes will be sampled for block colorization. Higher values greatly increase the amount of time it takes to build chunks for diminishing improvements in quality.
vitrine.options.entity_distance.name=Entity Distance
vitrine.options.entity_distance.tooltip=Controls how far away entities can render from the player. Higher values increase the render distance at the expense of frame rates.
vitrine.options.entity_shadows.tooltip=If enabled, basic shadows will be rendered beneath mobs and other entities.
vitrine.options.vignette.name=Vignette
vitrine.options.vignette.tooltip=If enabled, a vignette effect will be rendered on the player's view. This is very unlikely to make a difference to frame rates unless you are fill-rate limited.
vitrine.options.mipmap_levels.tooltip=Controls the number of mipmaps which will be used for block model textures. Higher values provide better rendering of blocks in the distance, but may adversely affect performance with many animated textures.
vitrine.options.animations.name=Animations
vitrine.options.animations.tooltip=If disabled, no animated texture will be updated and every texture stays on the frame it was showing. Animated textures can take a large share of each tick in packs that have many of them.
vitrine.options.animate_only_visible_textures.name=Animate Only Visible Textures
vitrine.options.animate_only_visible_textures.tooltip=If enabled, only animated textures determined to be visible will be updated. This can provide a significant boost to frame rates on some hardware, especially with heavier resource packs. If you experience issues with some textures not being animated, try disabling this option.
vitrine.options.animations.types=Textures
vitrine.options.animations.water.name=Water
vitrine.options.animations.water.tooltip=Animates the still and flowing water textures.
vitrine.options.animations.lava.name=Lava
vitrine.options.animations.lava.tooltip=Animates the still and flowing lava textures.
vitrine.options.animations.fire.name=Fire
vitrine.options.animations.fire.tooltip=Animates the fire texture, both on blocks and on burning entities.
vitrine.options.animations.portal.name=Nether Portal
vitrine.options.animations.portal.tooltip=Animates the Nether portal texture.
vitrine.options.animations.terrain.name=Blocks
vitrine.options.animations.terrain.tooltip=Animates every other block texture, including blocks added by mods.
vitrine.options.animations.textures.name=Items and Other
vitrine.options.animations.textures.tooltip=Animates textures that do not belong to blocks: items, the compass and the clock, and what mods draw themselves.
vitrine.options.particles.name=Particles
vitrine.options.particles.tooltip=If disabled, no particles will be spawned, including particles added by mods.
vitrine.options.particles.rain_splash.name=Rain Splashes
vitrine.options.particles.rain_splash.tooltip=Spawns splashes where rain lands on the ground, and smoke where it lands on lava. The rain itself and its sound are not affected.
vitrine.options.particles.block_break.name=Block Break
vitrine.options.particles.block_break.tooltip=Spawns particles when a block is broken.
vitrine.options.particles.block_breaking.name=Block Mining
vitrine.options.particles.block_breaking.tooltip=Spawns particles while a block is being mined.
